The web seat read docs/THE_PROGRAMME_IN_SHORT.md cold against its sources and found six lines that say more or less than
they do. Each is met here in the words of the full account (docs/THE_PROGRAMME_SO_FAR.md), which the lock checks:

1. The full account was checked line by line, in three parts, by three readers (its Appendix B), not each line by three.
2. The grammar is not stated as fact: each of its rules has a status, most assumed, one adopted by a decision (the full
   account says "by a ruling", a word the public face does not use), one chosen, one open (§ 2).
3. Each allowed word (a primitive word using both letters, § 3.1), not each word; a thread is one object the principle
   allows.
4. The root needs four inputs, each needed: the two selectors and two of the grammar's assumptions (GM3 and GM4, in
   plain words); and the figure-eight was named before the axioms, so the genesis is a conditional reconstruction of a
   chosen sector, not a derivation of m004 from nothing (§ 3.3).
5. The six mass ratios are reached only after choosing several inputs by hand or by looking at the data; and the quark
   mixing is either missed by the rigid versions of the frame or fitted by the free ones without being specific (§ 7).
6. Three gauge generations of chiral matter are not derived: the three of flavour is derived, and the three of gauge is
   a selection (§ 5.1).

THE LOCK, in tests/test_the_programme_so_far.py: each finding's new sentence on the page, its old wording gone, and each
new sentence found in the full account in its words; planted, four old wordings put back one at a time, each reported
alone. The page's own lock (a source for every line, no inner word) passes. BEFORE: on the tree before this patch, the
new test fails. Not read cold again yet: main's M30 asks for one more cold reading before the README points to the page.

0 of 19.
